{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790466516,"nonce":"ZWlxVOHLYad9Y5AYyou7JPVRlMc=","title":"Python: library loops keep calling back into the program after a callback raised","message":"A library function that calls back into the program keeps going after one\ncallback raised: `zb_list_sort_*` keeps comparing through\n`zb_hook_instance_lt`, `zb_list_map1`/`map2`/`filter`/`reduce` keep calling\nthe function value. The later callbacks run with py$exc set, which breaks\nthe entry contract (py$exc null at every function entry) that\nC-error-flag-fold relies on, and a callback with side effects runs when\nCPython would have stopped.\n\n```python\nclass Bad:\n    def __init__(self, v: int):\n        self.v = v\n    def __lt__(self, other) -\u003e bool:\n        if self.v == 3 or other.v == 3:\n            raise ValueError(\"cannot compare 3\")\n        return self.v \u003c other.v\n\ntry:\n    ys = sorted([Bad(1), Bad(3), Bad(2)])\n    print(\"after sorted\", len(ys))\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(\"ValueError:\", e)\n```\n\nOutput is right (the frontend checks after the sort), but\n`ZYNTAX_CHECK_ERROR_FLAG=1 ZYNTAX_BASELINE_THRESHOLD=1000000000 ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OSR=1`\naborts with `Bad$__lt__` entered with the error flag set. A raising key\nfunction shows the same whenever the key function reads the flag.\n\nThe stop has to be in zyntax_builtins and language neutral: when\n`Policy::exceptions` is set, the loops that call back test a pending hook\nafter each call and leave, or the frontend's ordering hooks return at once\nwith the flag set and carry an attribute exempting them from the entry\nassertion.","files":null}]}